None of these is built. The build uses ADAPTED copies, generated from the two
.s files by exact-match substitution (every changed line tagged [MODIFIED]):
  src/aes/aes128_ctr_m4ss.S     (T-table; included by aes128_ctr_m4ss_sram.S,
                                 aes128_ctr_m4ss_loop.S, aes128_ctr_m4ss_loop_sram.S)
  src/aes/aes128_ctr_m4ss_bs.S  (bitsliced)
with the C wrapper src/aes/aes128_m4ss.c. Their headers list the changes.

Upstream's published STM32F407 numbers were measured at 24 MHz with 0 flash
wait states (common/stm32f4_wrapper.c): 527.9 cycles/block (T-table CTR) and
1616.6 cycles/block (bitsliced CTR), averages over 4096-byte messages.

